<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' 1996 trade deficit at $11.8 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippines' 1996 trade deficit at $11.8 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines posted a merchandise trade deficit of $11.786 billion in 1996 against $9.091 billion in 1995, the National Stastics Office said on Friday.</p>
<p>The deficit was $835 million in December, from $950 million in the same month in 1995.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE	     Jan-Dec 96  Jan-Nov 96 Jan-Dec 95</p>
<p>	 Exports			  20.543     18.660	 17.447</p>
<p>	 Imports			  32.329     29.611	 26.538</p>
<p>	 Trade balance		 -11.786    -10.951	 -9.091</p>
<p>Note- Figures are in billion U.S. dollars.</p>
<p>				  - - - -</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE		  Dec 96     Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p>	 Exports			    1,883     1,850	 1,621</p>
<p>	 Imports			    2,718     2,711	 2,571</p>
<p>	 Trade balance		     -835	-861	  -950</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in million U.S. dollars. Components may not add up due to rounding off of figures.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8934</p>
</text>
